# Contributing to this leaderboard

This repository coordinates experiments for {{OBJECTIVE_NAME}}. The accountable owner is {{OWNER}}; accepted code is maintained by {{MAINTENANCE_TEAM}}.

Read `leaderboard/README.md` and `leaderboard/objective.yaml` first. For experiments follow `skills/benchcoding-contribute/SKILL.md`. Owners operating validation should follow `skills/benchcoding-maintain/SKILL.md`.

## Before running agents

Look at `leaderboard/board.md` and the linked experiments. Register your hypothesis through {{EXPERIMENT_ROUTE}}, linking related work and identifying your team, payer, starting baseline, and authorized budget. Check active claims and coordinate overlapping attempts through the collaboration route in `leaderboard/README.md`. Reuse failed findings instead of repeating an approach without a reason. Use only the data and resources allowed by the objective.

If the evaluation rules are unclear or cannot judge your proposed change, send the owner a concrete example and the missing decision before spending validation budget. Do not invent acceptance rules or silently change the evaluator. Record handoffs in the experiment with the current revision, findings, remaining budget, and next question.

## Submit evidence

Work from the recorded baseline in an isolated checkout. Record the harness/model, configuration, revisions, development evaluation, resource use, and findings. Local measurements are reported claims. Submit a pinned candidate through {{SUBMISSION_ROUTE}} and request validation through {{VALIDATION_ROUTE}}. An authorized owner admits it to the trusted queue. Record useful failures even when there is no code to merge.

Do not change the official evaluator, holdout, result records, or generated leaderboard as part of a candidate. Evaluator fixes go through separate owner review and versioning. Never make checks easier or omit difficult cases to improve a score. Do not expose restricted inputs, labels, credentials, or traces in issues or artifacts.

Stop when your allocation is exhausted. Do not repeatedly query acceptance evaluation or launch extra runs to get a favorable score. A verified result still requires integration review. Production changes and baseline promotion follow the owner's review process.

